SGP4/SDP4 in myb (ext/sgp4)

The theory is that of F. R. Hoots and R. L. Roehrich, "Models for Propagation of NORAD Element
Sets", Spacetrack Report #3 (U.S. Air Force, 1980), in the revision of D. A. Vallado,
P. Crawford, R. Hujsak and T. S. Kelso, "Revisiting Spacetrack Report #3", AIAA 2006-6753
(2006), whose reference code (SGP4.cpp, version of 12 March 2020) CelesTrak distributes for
free use.

sgp4.c is a C translation of that code made from its Python translation in python-sgp4 by
Brandon Rhodes (https://github.com/brandon-rhodes/python-sgp4, revision
8e234f81a93b226689a8b67d80a4f1a82be7439b, sgp4/propagation.py and sgp4/io.py), which is under the
